        "title": "Economic Geography",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Economic geography asks why economic activity concentrates where it does and\nwhat the implications of that concentration are for development, trade, and\ninequality. Agglomeration economies explain why Silicon Valley persists despite\nastronomical rents. World-systems theory explains why some places stay peripheral.\nThe container revolution explains modern trade geography. Supply chain\nvulnerabilities exposed by COVID and Suez are now reshaping the map."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-ECONOMIC-GEOGRAPHY.md#003",
      "path": [
        "07-ECONOMIC-GEOGRAPHY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
