      "text": "ALFRED WEBER (1909): Industrial Location:\n  Minimize total transport cost = (input materials to factory) +\n                                    (output products to market)\n  Material Index: weight of inputs / weight of outputs\n  High MI (>1): locate near raw materials (steel, cement, sugar refining)\n  Low MI (<1): locate near market (beer, bread — water added in production)\n  MI = 1: locate anywhere on transport cost gradient"
